\subsubsection{Migration from Vue2 to Vue3 and new trame best practices in the
trame tutorial}

Vue3 (and vuetify3 \cite{Vuetify}) is the new standard now that trame supports
it. The trame API also changed and a new standard was introduced, some syntax
changes were needed and some were strongly recommended to follow best practice.
The trame tutorial was the first thing to update. It was needed to change all
the examples in the
\href{https://github.com/Kitware/trame-tutorial}{trame-tutorial} repository, and
the corresponding \citev{VitePress} documentation in the
\href{https://github.com/Kitware/trame}{trame} repository.

\cref{pr:Kitware/trame-tutorial/7}, \cref{pr:Kitware/trame-tutorial/8},
\cref{pr:Kitware/trame-tutorial/9} and \cref{pr:Kitware/trame/877} are the Pull
Requests (PR) that make this change.


\subsubsection{Make all examples work}

Trame examples serve as a showcase for trame and show how it adapts with many
use cases and libraries, they also contain examples of usage of trame widgets.
They can serve as a starting point, for example, if someone wants to use
markdown with trame, they just have to copy the trame-markdown example.

\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/876} makes all the examples work. Most of the problems
came from changes in the APIs of imported modules as a proper requirements file
specifying module versions isn't provided, and this is intentional, since it's
better to keep examples that use libraries' last versions and features of
imported modules to show these libraries are compatible with trame.

As trame isn't yet fully documented with complete tutorials, there are many
features that one can only learn by watching example code so the examples are
complementary to the tutorial. This is why these examples were updated to use
the best practices just like in the precedent maintenance section.

\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/879} is just a fix because \cref{pr:Kitware/trame/876}
broke the documentation creation because of a typo and
\cref{pr:Kitware/trame/882}, \cref{pr:Kitware/trame/883} fix one last example
that used \citev{Docker} and \citev{ParaView}, an issue was created and then
closed for this fix
\href{https://github.com/Kitware/trame/issues/875}{trame/issues/875}

